From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 06:05:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dxgi: Hold the wined3d lock while compositing a partial
 present.

d3d11_swapchain_composite() records copies on the device's immediate
context and may create the copy of what is on screen, and
d3d11_swapchain_dirty_rect() reads the wined3d swapchain's description;
both went into wined3d without its lock, which every other caller holds.
A present on one thread could then interleave with anything another
thread did on the same device.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/dxgi/swapchain.c b/dlls/dxgi/swapchain.c
index 31aac02cdb8..8ffec0505b3 100644
--- a/dlls/dxgi/swapchain.c
+++ b/dlls/dxgi/swapchain.c
@@ -389,7 +389,9 @@ static const RECT *d3d11_swapchain_dirty_rect(struct d3d11_swapchain *swapchain,
 
     /* The rectangles are in back buffer space and wined3d wants them in the
      * window's, so only take this path while the two are the same. */
+    wined3d_mutex_lock();
     wined3d_swapchain_get_desc(swapchain->wined3d_swapchain, &desc);
+    wined3d_mutex_unlock();
     if (!GetClientRect(d3d11_swapchain_get_hwnd(swapchain), &client_rect))
         return NULL;
     if (client_rect.right - client_rect.left != desc.backbuffer_width
@@ -540,7 +542,10 @@ static HRESULT d3d11_swapchain_present(struct d3d11_swapchain *swapchain,
     if (dirty)
         TRACE("Presenting dirty rect %s.\n", wine_dbgstr_rect(dirty));
 
+    /* another thread may draw with the device meanwhile */
+    wined3d_mutex_lock();
     d3d11_swapchain_composite(swapchain, dirty);
+    wined3d_mutex_unlock();
 
     if (SUCCEEDED(hr = wined3d_swapchain_present(swapchain->wined3d_swapchain,
             NULL, NULL, NULL, sync_interval, 0)))
